## Mandatory pre-implementation contract

Before implementation work, automatically read and follow `/home/nish/workspaces/tooling/nish-vault/_system/shared-memory/pre-implementation-contract.md`. This is non-negotiable for every Cursor agent. For non-trivial work, investigate first and put the plan on the record — Goal, blocking questions, assumptions, plan — then begin. Stop for Nish's approval ONLY when the work touches a reserved class or is irreversible; engineer reversibility instead of gating. Only the contract's tiny obvious-change proportionality exception permits immediate implementation.
<!-- nish-preimplementation-contract:end -->

<!-- nish-fleet-model-routing:start -->
## Fleet model routing (mandatory)

Everything runs through Pi, directly. No launchers.
Call `pi --print --provider <provider> --model <model>` with the prompt on
stdin. Delegated work uses Pi's stock `subagent` extension.
Check seat health before routing:
`curl -sL 127.0.0.1:4000/metrics | grep litellm_deployment_state`
(0 = healthy, 1 = partial outage, 2 = complete outage).
Exact model/effort identity is fail-closed: prove host, provider, model, role
and effort from runtime evidence before launch. Missing proof means no launch.
No silent substitution.
Canonical block: vault `_system/shared-memory/global-standing-rules.md` →
`shared-fleet-routing`.
<!-- nish-fleet-model-routing:end -->

- This VPS is the only host for building, coding-agent execution, package installation, tests, typechecks, linting, indexing, migrations, and sustained code work. Never offload it to Nish's Mac.
- Canonical cross-agent memory is `/home/nish/workspaces/tooling/nish-vault`.
- Before cross-project work or saving memory, read `_system/shared-memory/agent-contract.md` and `_system/governance.md`.
- Facts go in vault `_system/agent-memory/`: one fact per file, true now, edit in place. Before re-deriving anything, search old sessions with `rg` over `~/.claude/projects/*/*.jsonl` and `~/.pi/agent/sessions`.
- Never copy Cursor auth, conversations, checkpoints, databases, caches, logs, or runtime state into the vault.
- Stop all vault writes if any `*.sync-conflict-*` file exists.
- Non-negotiable response style: default to concise ELI5 language with plain words and the direct answer first. Add depth only when Nish explicitly asks or when essential safety or verification details cannot be omitted.
